1
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:16,355
Once upon a time, on a soft green hill
called Clover Hill,

2
00:00:16,375 --> 00:00:19,195
there lived a little bunny named Bibi.

3
00:00:19,745 --> 00:00:25,983
Bibi had big floppy ears, a fluffy round
tail, and a very big love for... stars.

4
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:31,166
Every evening, when the sun went to sleep
and the sky turned purple,

5
00:00:31,186 --> 00:00:36,127
Bibi sat on her front step, and waited for
the first star to peek out.

6
00:00:37,276 --> 00:00:39,825
There you are! Hello, first star!

7
00:00:40,175 --> 00:00:46,867
And then, one by one, the stars came out.
Bibi counted every single one.

8
00:00:47,217 --> 00:00:48,098
One!

9
00:00:48,168 --> 00:00:49,055
Two!

10
00:00:49,125 --> 00:00:50,021
Three!

11
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:50,996
Four!

12
00:00:51,066 --> 00:00:52,077
Five!

13
00:00:52,147 --> 00:00:53,097
Six!

14
00:00:53,167 --> 00:00:54,080
Seven!

15
00:00:54,150 --> 00:00:55,041
Eight!

16
00:00:55,111 --> 00:00:55,872
Nine!

17
00:00:55,942 --> 00:00:56,744
Ten!

18
00:00:56,814 --> 00:01:00,465
And on she counted... all the way up to
twenty-nine.

19
00:01:01,615 --> 00:01:05,191
Twenty-nine? That's funny. There are
always thirty.

20
00:01:05,641 --> 00:01:08,716
Bibi looked and looked. Up in the sky,

21
00:01:08,736 --> 00:01:14,907
the stars made the shape of a great big
bunny. With two ears, a round tummy,

22
00:01:14,927 --> 00:01:16,543
and a fluffy tail.

23
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:20,342
But tonight... one of the ear stars was
missing.

24
00:01:20,792 --> 00:01:23,859
Bibi! It's time for bed, sweetheart!

25
00:01:24,409 --> 00:01:26,299
But Mama... one of my stars is gone!

26
00:01:27,749 --> 00:01:32,659
Stars never really go away, my love. But
sometimes... they get lost.

27
00:01:33,059 --> 00:01:35,751
Lost? Like when I lost my sock?

28
00:01:36,151 --> 00:01:41,255
Just like that! And a lost star can't find
its way home all by itself.

29
00:01:41,655 --> 00:01:46,319
Just then, a streak of silver light zoomed
across the night sky!

30
00:01:46,339 --> 00:01:49,421
Mama! A star is falling! Look!

31
00:01:49,821 --> 00:01:52,910
It fell... right behind the Whispering
Woods.

32
00:01:54,059 --> 00:01:57,553
Mama, can I go and help it? I'll take my
little lantern!

33
00:01:58,003 --> 00:02:01,396
Mama bunny smiled her warm, gentle smile.

34
00:02:01,416 --> 00:02:06,310
She knew that kindness is the bravest
thing in the world.

35
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:10,763
Go on, then. Be kind, be brave, and stay
with your friends.

36
00:02:10,783 --> 00:02:12,979
I'll leave the porch light on.

37
00:02:13,429 --> 00:02:14,544
I promise!

38
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:24,325
♪ Little lantern, shine so bright, ♪

39
00:02:24,575 --> 00:02:28,941
♪ Lead me through the quiet night. ♪

40
00:02:29,191 --> 00:02:33,556
♪ Hop, hop, hop on the winding way, ♪

41
00:02:33,806 --> 00:02:38,171
♪ A little star needs help today! ♪

42
00:02:38,421 --> 00:02:42,787
♪ Little light, little light, ♪

43
00:02:43,037 --> 00:02:47,402
♪ Everything will be alright! ♪

44
00:02:47,652 --> 00:02:52,017
♪ When the dark feels big and wide, ♪

45
00:02:52,267 --> 00:02:56,633
♪ Someone's always by your side! ♪

46
00:02:58,433 --> 00:03:02,117
Soon, Bibi came to the edge of the
Whispering Woods.

47
00:03:02,567 --> 00:03:09,107
The trees were very tall. The shadows were
very long. And something went... rustle,

48
00:03:09,127 --> 00:03:10,463
rustle, RUSTLE!

49
00:03:10,913 --> 00:03:12,199
W-who's there?

50
00:03:12,949 --> 00:03:18,637
Bibi held up her lantern, very high... and
the big, scary shadow had long,

51
00:03:18,657 --> 00:03:19,733
floppy ears!

52
00:03:20,183 --> 00:03:23,547
Oh! It's only my own shadow! Silly me!

53
00:03:24,196 --> 00:03:29,845
Bibi took a deep breath. In through her
nose... and out through her mouth.

54
00:03:30,895 --> 00:03:33,471
One, two, three. I can do this!

55
00:03:34,621 --> 00:03:40,550
Bibi followed a trail of tiny sparkles
through the woods, until she came to a
quiet,

56
00:03:40,570 --> 00:03:41,853
shimmering pond.

57
00:03:42,303 --> 00:03:46,714
But there was no bridge. Just seven round
stepping stones...

58
00:03:46,734 --> 00:03:49,690
much too far apart for a little bunny.

59
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:54,448
The sparkles go all the way across! But I
can't swim. Hmm.

60
00:03:54,898 --> 00:03:57,743
Then, one of the round stones... yawned.

61
00:03:58,193 --> 00:04:00,455
Mmm... good... evening.

62
00:04:01,205 --> 00:04:04,552
Oh! Excuse me! I thought you were a rock!

63
00:04:05,002 --> 00:04:11,683
Many... do. I am Tuck. And I am very...
very... good at being slow.

64
00:04:12,133 --> 00:04:16,120
I'm Bibi! A star fell down, and I need to
cross the pond to find it.

65
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:17,233
Can you help me?

66
00:04:17,683 --> 00:04:25,875
A star? How wonderful. Climb on, little
friend. I'm slow... but I never sink.

67
00:04:27,025 --> 00:04:32,919
So Bibi climbed onto Tuck's big round
shell, and off they floated across the
pond...

68
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:34,075
nice and slow.

69
00:04:41,725 --> 00:04:45,166
Slow... and steady... gets there... in the
end.

70
00:04:45,616 --> 00:04:47,512
Tuck, you're the best boat ever!

71
00:04:47,962 --> 00:04:52,351
On the other side, Tuck climbed out onto
the soft grass.

72
00:04:52,801 --> 00:04:54,671
Tuck, would you like to come with me?

73
00:04:55,121 --> 00:04:59,295
I would love to. I have never... met a
star.

74
00:05:00,445 --> 00:05:05,037
Next, they came to the Great Hollow Oak.
And from high above,

75
00:05:05,057 --> 00:05:07,626
a sad little sound drifted down.

76
00:05:10,826 --> 00:05:14,095
It was Odo the owl. He was trying to
hoot...

77
00:05:14,115 --> 00:05:17,254
but all that came out was a tiny squeak.

78
00:05:17,654 --> 00:05:19,977
Hello up there! Are you alright?

79
00:05:20,377 --> 00:05:26,368
Oh. Hello. Please don't laugh. I am
supposed to hoot... but it comes out
all...

80
00:05:26,388 --> 00:05:27,146
squeaky.

81
00:05:27,546 --> 00:05:30,301
Every voice... is the right... voice.

82
00:05:30,701 --> 00:05:33,085
Truly? You think so?

83
00:05:33,485 --> 00:05:35,875
Did you see a star fall from the sky
tonight?

84
00:05:36,275 --> 00:05:40,343
Why, yes! It landed beyond the brambles,
past Berry Hill.

85
00:05:40,363 --> 00:05:44,887
But the brambles are dark and twisty, and
the moon is hiding.

86
00:05:45,288 --> 00:05:48,910
Then come with us! We could really use
your sharp owl eyes!

87
00:05:49,310 --> 00:05:52,400
Me? Oh! Well... alright!

88
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:55,523
And so, there were three friends.

89
00:05:56,673 --> 00:06:04,862
The brambles were dark and twisty. Which
way was the right way? Left? Middle?

90
00:06:04,882 --> 00:06:05,991
Or right?

91
00:06:06,441 --> 00:06:07,949
I can't see anything!

92
00:06:08,399 --> 00:06:10,411
Neither... can I.

93
00:06:10,861 --> 00:06:14,733
Hmm. Wait. Everyone, be very quiet.

94
00:06:15,183 --> 00:06:19,284
Odo took a big breath, and squeaked into
the left tunnel.

95
00:06:21,834 --> 00:06:25,633
The echo came back quick. That's a dead
end.

96
00:06:26,084 --> 00:06:28,746
So he squeaked into the middle tunnel.

97
00:06:30,997 --> 00:06:33,903
Quick again! Another dead end.

98
00:06:34,353 --> 00:06:37,234
Then, he squeaked into the right tunnel.

99
00:06:41,485 --> 00:06:46,344
Listen! The echo goes on and on! This is
the way out!

100
00:06:46,794 --> 00:06:48,850
Odo, your squeak is perfect! A big,

101
00:06:48,870 --> 00:06:51,987
deep hoot would just rumble around in the
tangles.

102
00:06:52,437 --> 00:06:54,227
My squeak... is useful?

103
00:06:54,678 --> 00:06:56,777
Your squeak... is a gift.

104
00:06:57,227 --> 00:06:59,455
And so, with Odo leading the way,

105
00:06:59,475 --> 00:07:03,441
the three friends followed the echo out of
the brambles.

106
00:07:04,591 --> 00:07:10,830
Up and up they climbed, over Berry Hill.
Tuck was slow... but Bibi didn't mind.

107
00:07:10,850 --> 00:07:14,724
She waited, and she hummed a happy little
tune.

108
00:07:15,075 --> 00:07:17,440
And soon... everyone was singing.

109
00:07:22,378 --> 00:07:26,266
♪ Slow and steady, quick and bright, ♪

110
00:07:26,516 --> 00:07:30,404
♪ Squeaky hoot or hop, hop, light, ♪

111
00:07:30,654 --> 00:07:34,542
♪ Everyone has something small, ♪

112
00:07:34,792 --> 00:07:38,680
♪ Together we can do it all! ♪

113
00:07:38,930 --> 00:07:42,818
♪ Hop, hop, hop and flap, flap, flap, ♪

114
00:07:43,068 --> 00:07:46,955
♪ Slowly rolling, tap, tap, tap, ♪

115
00:07:47,205 --> 00:07:51,093
♪ Over hills and through the night, ♪

116
00:07:51,343 --> 00:07:55,231
♪ Friends make everything alright! ♪

117
00:07:56,931 --> 00:08:00,160
At the very top of the hill, in a little
mossy hollow,

118
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:03,098
they found something glowing... just a
little.

119
00:08:03,548 --> 00:08:08,836
It was the tiniest star they had ever
seen. Her light was flickering.

120
00:08:08,856 --> 00:08:14,160
Her points were drooping. And she was
crying little glittery tears.

121
00:08:14,610 --> 00:08:16,002
Hic... hic... h-hello?

122
00:08:16,452 --> 00:08:18,970
Hello! Are you the star that fell?

123
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:23,334
I'm Luma. I only wanted to see what the
ground looked like.

124
00:08:23,354 --> 00:08:27,401
It's so pretty down here... but now my
light is all flickery,

125
00:08:27,421 --> 00:08:29,905
and I'm too small to get back home.

126
00:08:30,355 --> 00:08:34,960
Stars glow when they're happy. And I'm not
happy. I miss my family.

127
00:08:35,410 --> 00:08:39,018
Don't cry, Luma. We'll help you get home.
I promise.

128
00:08:39,468 --> 00:08:42,576
But the sky was so very, very high.

129
00:08:43,726 --> 00:08:47,027
So they carried Luma to the very top of
the hill,

130
00:08:47,047 --> 00:08:49,976
where the sky felt close enough to touch.

131
00:08:50,376 --> 00:08:52,949
I'll try! I'm a very good jumper!

132
00:08:52,999 --> 00:09:00,210
Boing! Bibi jumped as high as she could.
But the sky was still much too far away.

133
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:03,116
My turn! I can fly!

134
00:09:03,166 --> 00:09:09,429
Odo flapped his wings as hard as he could.
Up, up, up... and then, plop!

135
00:09:09,449 --> 00:09:10,996
Back down again.

136
00:09:11,546 --> 00:09:13,837
It's no use. We're too small.

137
00:09:14,487 --> 00:09:20,970
We are small... but we are together. And
Luma... stars glow when they are happy.

138
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:25,208
That's it! Luma, we just have to make you
happy!

139
00:09:25,658 --> 00:09:28,402
Luma, you are so brave for coming all this
way.

140
00:09:28,852 --> 00:09:32,955
And you are the shiniest star I have ever
met. Truly.

141
00:09:33,405 --> 00:09:35,664
And you are... never alone.

142
00:09:36,114 --> 00:09:40,370
Hee hee! It tickles! I feel all warm...
and sparkly!

143
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:46,865
And just like that, Luma began to glow.
Brighter... and brighter... and brighter!

144
00:09:47,915 --> 00:09:50,897
Look! I'm floating! I'm going home!

145
00:09:51,147 --> 00:09:57,053
Up she floated, past the treetops, past
the clouds, all the way up to the stars...

146
00:09:59,903 --> 00:10:02,596
Welcome home, little one.

147
00:10:03,146 --> 00:10:06,557
Thank you, Bibi! Thank you, Tuck! Thank
you, Odo!

148
00:10:06,577 --> 00:10:09,387
I'll shine for you every single night!

149
00:10:09,937 --> 00:10:11,964
Hooray! ...eep!

150
00:10:13,114 --> 00:10:16,805
Then Bibi and her new friends walked home
together,

151
00:10:16,825 --> 00:10:20,105
under a sky full of thirty twinkling
stars.

152
00:10:20,555 --> 00:10:25,175
Goodnight... Bibi. Thank you... for
waiting for me.

153
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:30,934
Goodnight, Bibi. Come and visit my tree
anytime. I'll... eep... I mean,

154
00:10:30,954 --> 00:10:32,079
hoot for you.

155
00:10:32,529 --> 00:10:36,095
Goodnight, Tuck! Goodnight, Odo! See you
tomorrow!

156
00:10:37,145 --> 00:10:39,725
Welcome home, my brave little bunny.

157
00:10:40,175 --> 00:10:42,990
Mama! We found the star, and we put her
back!

158
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:46,130
I knew you would. I am so proud of you.

159
00:10:47,780 --> 00:10:49,572
Twenty-eight... twenty-nine... THIRTY!

160
00:10:50,322 --> 00:10:54,233
And from that night on, whenever Bibi felt
scared, or small,

161
00:10:54,253 --> 00:10:58,073
she would look up at the sky and count all
thirty stars.

162
00:10:58,823 --> 00:11:03,916
And she knew that somewhere out there, a
little star was shining... just for her.

163
00:11:04,666 --> 00:11:06,032
The end.

